ople do go  in support of protecting  abortion rights and procedures  what more can be done by  representatives at this point if you're  expecting that it will be overturned and  what do you say to people who are  concerned uh and those who are rejoicing  this morning  well first of all i think we need to  once again bring the women's protection  health protection act up for a vote that  would guarantee that roe v wade would be  the law of the land and as i've said our  republican colleagues have very sadly  for the women of america  been blocking that from coming up to a  vote but i  i believe we need to immediately call it  up for a vote again it has passed in the  house of representatives and it's time  in the senate to call it up for a vote  the other thing that can happen is it's  state legislatures across the country  the fight will be fought  this will of course result in a  patchwork of laws but for anyone that's  just been believing that we can sit on  our laurels of a 50-year opinion that  all the work from the past  is behind us it's not in fact the work  has just begun i remember once barbara  mikulski who was the dean of the women  of the senate would always say  suit up um suit up  put your shoulders straight put your  lipstick on and get ready for a fight  because that is exactly what's gonna  happen with the women of america and we  simply can't let this court which is so  out of step with the people of america  and if this leaked opinion is true they  are literally overturning a 50 years of  precedent  if with a case that is supported by 80  of the american public just because they  have their own personal political views  because you can and we have no idea what  floodgate will be open on birth control  and the like uh we have republican uh  legislators that are talking about  six-week fan on abortion this is going  to be complete chaos if this goes  through  senator klobuchar you mentioned the  american people and wishful thinking is  we agree upon a law and there's  uniformity across the country that's not  the case so with that said previous  polling shows that majority of people  from certain states they are against  abortion so there is a thought out there  that if that is the case then why  shouldn't abortion laws just be left up  to the states what do you say to that  okay nate well first of all the numbers  nationwide are somewhere between 75 to  80 percent of the people poll and poll  again have shown that 75 to 80 percent  of the people believe that a woman  should have the right to make her own  decisions reproductive decisions  different states of course you're going  to get different numbers but the beauty  of having this done through a court  opinion because it was seen as such a  fundamental right written a case written  by a republican appointed supreme court  justice justice blackman 50 years ago  he looked at it and he said look i was  appointed by a republican but i believe  when i look at the constitution and what  has been happening in america that this  is a fundamental right just like birth  control was found to be a fundamental  right the world changes and it's the  supreme court's job to interpret the  laws as there are the constitution as it  is to see if it includes fundamental  rights that's what gay marriage was all  about so if this court is going to turn  back the clock and take away all of  these rights that have been considered  in well-thought-out cases we have  basically a revolution going on when it  comes to women's rights and people are  going to have to go to the ballot box  and make that decision and yeah you're  right those states will have the  opportunity to do that some of them  already have like texas where they've  established bounty hunters so you can  tell on your neighbor and call them out  i just don't think that's the future we  want  yeah senator it certainly does change  the politics of the midterm uh that  that's for sure it's 50 years now almost  of a guaranteed constitutional right of  access to abortion in this country which  may end uh in the not-too-distant future  thank you for crystallizing the  conversation for us senator klobuchar  appreciate it thank you

